cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "MAG-S2: the shape of the quantum compass signal"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikabri88-cmd/quantum-compass-topology"
authors:
  - family-names: Ryzhkova
    given-names: Julia
    affiliation: Siriona
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4194-6059"
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered simulation study of the shape of neural population activity that reads a radical-pair
  (cryptochrome) magnetic compass. The singlet yield of a radical pair is the same for a field and for the reversed
  field, so the population lies on the real projective plane RP2, while a polarity-sensitive control read by the
  same eyes and neurons gives a sphere. Persistent homology with Z2 and Z3 coefficients tells the two shapes apart.
  In the confirmatory run on ten simulated birds all invariants held and all expectations and hypotheses were met:
  the intact compass was labelled RP2 in 10 of 10 birds, the polar control a sphere in 10 of 10, head rotations about
  the vertical axis a ring in 10 of 10 at inclination 66 degrees and at the magnetic equator, and a heading decoder
  confused headings 180 degrees apart at the equator and kept them apart at inclination 66 degrees. Code is released
  under MIT; text, figures, the protocol and the results are released under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - magnetoreception
  - radical pair
  - cryptochrome
  - persistent homology
  - topological data analysis
  - neural manifold
  - projective plane
  - pre-registration
  - simulation
